%description:
Tests a CE-marked SYN in AccECN. The server feeds back the CE mark with
(AE,CWR,ECE) = (1,1,0) on the SYN-ACK (RFC 9768 Table 2). The counter of the
client stays at 5 (section 3.2.2.2), but the client responds to the
congestion at the first ACK of its data: ssthresh becomes 1024.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.tcptester.script="a1 ce"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S E W N 0:0(0) win 16384 CE   Option(s): MaxSegSize# marking CE
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[0.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S W N 500:500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: A W ack 501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 ECT(0) 
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N ack 1001 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
AccECN-setup SYN-ACK packet received (ACE=6, IP ECN 0)... AccECN is enabled.
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
AccECN: ACE=5, packets acknowledged=1, new CE marks=0 (mod 8: 0)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
cwnd = cwnd / 2: received ECN-Echo ACK... new cwnd = 1024
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
ssthresh = cwnd: received ECN-Echo ACK... new ssthresh = 1024
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
